{"title":"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(utterly_disgusting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (utterly disgusting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f4b10f1bbab2d159a8c5749bc1163291517b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\le \\theta &lt; 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />, let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a690d6e3555b1b58448f66797e18b88bc5f59e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P &amp;= \\frac12\\cos\\theta - \\frac14\\sin 2\\theta - \\frac18\\cos 3\\theta + \\frac{1}{16}\\sin 4\\theta + \\frac{1}{32} \\cos 5\\theta - \\frac{1}{64} \\sin 6\\theta - \\frac{1}{128} \\cos 7\\theta + \\cdots \\end{align*}\" width=\"674\" height=\"37\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f8176bb53e9c424986b76b9b528021956685209e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} Q &amp;= 1 - \\frac12\\sin\\theta -\\frac14\\cos 2\\theta + \\frac18 \\sin 3\\theta + \\frac{1}{16}\\cos 4\\theta - \\frac{1}{32}\\sin 5\\theta - \\frac{1}{64}\\cos 6\\theta +\\frac{1}{128}\\sin 7\\theta + \\cdots \\end{align*}\" width=\"704\" height=\"37\" />\nso that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fde379d11cb11c02933435678daf54006f31e72b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{P}{Q} = \\frac{2\\sqrt2}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"78\" height=\"44\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/8911f61bda61eb80e4e98062ff0dcd20103200b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta = -\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"91\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Noticing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> in both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5646f1d6eed76fee4840dacf4c8fb39ef64fe46e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> we think of the angle addition identities: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/f/37fb8049a1fcba8424e9b4a24dd0faad1a5f01ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(a + b) = \\sin a \\cos b + \\cos a \\sin b, \\cos(a + b) = \\cos a \\cos b - \\sin a \\sin b\\]\" width=\"515\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>With this in mind, we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/865211471c7cc8aff3d88f9f2b843bd262159050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> to try and use some angle addition identities. Indeed, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/2/772ed85019fd93bf025dafcb5f86a409d732571a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P \\sin \\theta + Q \\cos \\theta &amp;= \\cos \\theta + \\dfrac{1}{2}(\\cos \\theta \\sin \\theta - \\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta) - \\dfrac{1}{4}(\\sin{2 \\theta} \\sin \\theta + \\cos{2 \\theta} \\cos{\\theta}) - \\cdots \\\\ &amp;= \\cos \\theta - \\dfrac{1}{4} \\cos \\theta + \\dfrac{1}{8} \\sin{2 \\theta} + \\dfrac{1}{16} \\cos{3 \\theta} + \\cdots \\\\ &amp;= \\cos \\theta - \\dfrac{1}{2}P \\end{align*}\" width=\"686\" height=\"123\" />\nafter adding term-by-term. Similar term-by-term adding yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7f0b9278885701dc720d88cad9b55141353f5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P \\cos \\theta + Q \\sin \\theta = -2(Q - 1).\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"18\" /> \nThis is a system of equations; rearrange and rewrite to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/0/b90ddfc73ef18a50c47a94998f40afd23d86c9ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(1 + 2 \\sin \\theta) + 2Q \\cos \\theta = 2 \\cos \\theta\\]\" width=\"263\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8ebc6648cff0d2b1b480f736de2b188b3a8ad00f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P \\cos^2 \\theta + Q \\cos \\theta(2 + \\sin \\theta) = 2 \\cos \\theta.\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"19\" /> Subtract the two and rearrange to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/a/d9a50cf3cf3a262e6e770559523ea1e76fc92596.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{P}{Q} = \\dfrac{\\cos \\theta}{2 + \\sin \\theta} = \\dfrac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{7}.\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"44\" /> Then, square both sides and use Pythagorean Identity to get a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f156b7740d026834984824b21fd2ac270c0176e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta.$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> Factor that quadratic and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bf11ae84579b4a0f31063604c631f4e75071777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = -17/19, 1/3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> Since we're given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57763fa92118d2436542c30418070ea1fac9034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi\\leq\\theta&lt;2\\pi,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cc6cd401ab7d1f6f198d8b36a1e53d6403555e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta$\" width=\"34\" height=\"13\" /> is nonpositive. We therefore use the negative solution, and our desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82fec736b88ddad84b911090c9bb24b737a1771.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 + 19 = \\boxed{036}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use sum to product formulas to rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fff97ae90adf34f8c6496cbffc9dee3d556e2ca5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P \\sin\\theta\\ + Q \\cos\\theta\\ = \\cos \\theta\\ - \\frac{1}{4}\\cos \\theta + \\frac{1}{8}\\sin 2\\theta + \\frac{1}{16}\\cos 3\\theta - \\frac{1}{32}\\sin 4\\theta + ...\\]\" width=\"526\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b56f2b8ce3319c2d27ec3d2c70e4cd40b0131437.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P \\sin \\theta - Q \\cos \\theta = -2P\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/584e152296a27a82e657528b2359c36dbee5af07.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{P}{Q} =  \\frac{2\\sqrt2}{7}, Q = \\frac{7}{2\\sqrt2} P\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Plug in to the previous equation and cancel out the \"P\" terms to get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6f7e2d3a4ddfe048f02345e7979fa6490a1409a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin\\theta - \\frac{7}{2\\sqrt2} \\cos\\theta = -2\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Then use the pythagorean identity to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cc6cd401ab7d1f6f198d8b36a1e53d6403555e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta$\" width=\"34\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/7402fb2c25bb2e84914cda695e5f23007d2a63b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin\\theta = -\\frac{17}{19} \\implies \\boxed{036}\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82a6484836de605d97757f335cf88350a6ba0ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[e^{i\\theta}=\\cos(\\theta)+i\\sin(\\theta)\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the following identities follow immediately:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5aeba9631068b4cc051cdc4053d3508d73f0154a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ie^{i\\theta}=i(\\cos(\\theta)+i\\sin(\\theta))=-\\sin(\\theta)+i\\cos(\\theta)\\]\" width=\"360\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/7/a676f6a4ce6d1cbf0b47de643616658a1f7b3a5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[i^2 e^{i\\theta}=-e^{i\\theta}=-\\cos(\\theta)-i\\sin(\\theta)\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f6c408f5a69f99ef3e629b84218905fcfef5b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[i^3 e^{i\\theta}=\\sin(\\theta)-i\\cos(\\theta)\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Consider, now, the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebd3eff720661f50e93ee0a81bcddd545359d390.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q+iP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" />. It follows fairly immediately that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b9648f1b7d8f909195f14f24132ade91f23f1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q+iP=1+\\left(\\frac{i}{2}\\right)^1e^{i\\theta}+\\left(\\frac{i}{2}\\right)^2e^{2i\\theta}+\\ldots=\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{i}{2}e^{i\\theta}}=\\frac{2}{2-ie^{i\\theta}}\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"48\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cdeb0c3f45c57255ba50e3b5de528ba0501afc2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q+iP=\\frac{2}{2-ie^{i\\theta}}=\\frac{2}{2-(-\\sin(\\theta)+i\\cos(\\theta))}=\\frac{2}{(2+\\sin(\\theta))-i\\cos(\\theta)}\\]\" width=\"546\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>This follows straight from the geometric series formula and simple simplification. We can now multiply the denominator by it's complex conjugate to find:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fcc16b32c0630fd63c8b0ba371fb08bf935fc47.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q+iP=\\frac{2}{(2+\\sin(\\theta))-i\\cos(\\theta)}\\left(\\frac{(2+\\sin(\\theta))+i\\cos(\\theta)}{(2+\\sin(\\theta))+i\\cos(\\theta)}\\right)\\]\" width=\"454\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dceef385104597a0c227b9af4a8f127118e7befa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q+iP=\\frac{2((2+\\sin(\\theta))+i\\cos(\\theta))}{(2+\\sin(\\theta))^2+\\cos^2(\\theta)}\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Comparing real and imaginary parts, we find:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0ad275819f665b491cc430ef60d2a1a865615d00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{P}{Q}=\\frac{\\cos(\\theta)}{2+\\sin(\\theta)}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{7}\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Squaring this equation and letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7f66e888b70d39cc49cc202d24596993537a036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(\\theta)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec3b6a038a7c4ad08c8c6ae0bed0f02d61eaca6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{P^2}{Q^2}=\\frac{\\cos^2(\\theta)}{4+4\\sin(\\theta)+\\sin^2(\\theta)}=\\frac{1-x^2}{4+4x+x^2}=\\frac{8}{49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"382\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Clearing denominators and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives sine as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d023b0356935e1186312628d94cae23af742bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac{17}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/40389ac37d97754a42ef5b2aaac571cf839067df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$017+019=\\boxed{036}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bit similar to Solution 3. We use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/116d9001403ff80aa679aee5490906de76458769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi = \\theta+90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> because the progression cycles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/5903dcce8ca1b35232ba20578615e9f1d5c308b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P\\in (\\sin 0\\theta,\\cos 1\\theta,-\\sin 2\\theta,-\\cos 3\\theta\\dots)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"313\" height=\"18\" />. So we could rewrite that as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7a7e24fb1be1a9c967797ed9447b5204676973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P\\in(\\sin 0\\phi,\\sin 1\\phi,\\sin 2\\phi,\\sin 3\\phi\\dots)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"281\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39ad063f6459363bd267c0118df4b1fbd2e9249d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q\\in (\\cos 0\\theta,-\\sin 1\\theta,-\\cos 2\\theta,\\sin 3\\theta\\dots)\\implies Q\\in(\\cos 0\\phi,\\cos 1\\phi, \\cos 2\\phi, \\cos 3\\phi\\dots)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"654\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Setting complex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/30357da8d5f69b6363b227168d5b1cca6f365270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=q_1+p_1i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/d/d7dc8c7dc9754f5f80fac48613c7433525af36fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\cos\\phi+\\sin\\phi i\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"165\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55cb3d42ed5b90eab6032a0e704871482a51191b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(Q,P)=\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty z^n=\\frac{1}{1-z}=\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos\\phi-\\frac{i}{2}\\sin\\phi}=\\frac{1-0.5\\cos\\phi+0.5i\\sin\\phi}{\\dots}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"587\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>The important part is the ratio of the imaginary part <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> to the real part. To cancel out the imaginary part from the denominator, we must add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad249efcc07ddcba003dc298f517d30c6e809085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5i\\sin\\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> to the numerator to make the denominator a difference (or rather a sum) of squares. The denominator does not matter. Only the numerator, because we are trying to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/469e5782d60ae35bd7e8b27cf0309c6a1704bc95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{P}{Q}=\\tan\\text{arg}(\\Sigma)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"120\" height=\"41\" /> a PROPORTION of values. So denominators would cancel out.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815f8a15e6365b8ed1529b25b119579b9aa7ff2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{P}{Q}=\\frac{\\text{Re}\\Sigma}{\\text{Im}\\Sigma}=\\frac{0.5\\sin\\phi}{1-0.5\\cos\\phi}=\\frac{\\sin\\phi}{2-\\cos\\phi}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"361\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c47fdd44d213f9ae05cb51fe897c0d0b9e3cb00e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" />, we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/4/b749b1add6d487b5f48ad07cd195f25dc73482b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{1-y^2}}{2+y}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{7}\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d7758255ee954046d7388490c690a6834653b398.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7\\sqrt{1-y^2}=2\\sqrt{2}(2+y)\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"22\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a8afe387d2e523f03f7f04907111781e67f3a03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[49-49y^2=8y^2+32y+32\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/0/c107b63cc0dd44407ba0ddebca77d2044a6f0984.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[57y^2+32y-17=0\\rightarrow y=\\frac{-32\\pm\\sqrt{1024+4\\cdot 969}}{114}\\]\" width=\"400\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e59437e0ed9d7913aff573ecb9e2d69220d86e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\frac{-32\\pm\\sqrt{4900}}{114}=\\frac{-16\\pm 35}{57}\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14fdb7fc1a58d1fa221727ace4b9cd7ddc35eeb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be6527cbc54cf34cb53076083ce9739bf1e3757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi&lt;\\theta&lt;2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccd77e7e2758a722a8daa0dc02af2624804318c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sin\\theta=-\\frac{51}{57}=-\\frac{17}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"187\" height=\"38\" />. Adding up, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904c49894e7b5e64875e93edfc386cc3b79bd389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17+19=\\boxed{036}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28utterly_disgusting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(utterly_disgusting)\">Solution 5 (utterly disgusting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (utterly disgusting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/449179e645e0fe6604765f13887efc70cebee10a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta=-\\frac{i}{2}(e^{i\\theta}-e^{-i\\theta})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/2/1a2e15604eef9eb92eaad69174f226289906d7e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta=\\frac{1}{2}(e^{i\\theta}+e^{-i\\theta})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"160\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>We observe that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> can be split into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> parts, namely the terms which contain the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> and the terms which contain the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a9f129d2cad1186b25ba06662846c63cedbbcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin .$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d48b69da65b3a0a7b9b2db907cd09811dcae30b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac12\\cos\\theta-\\frac18\\cos3\\theta+\\cdots&amp;=\\frac14\\left(e^{i\\theta}\\left(1-\\frac{e^{i2\\theta}}{4}+\\cdots\\right)+e^{-i\\theta}\\left(1-\\frac{e^{-i2\\theta}}{4}+\\cdots\\right)\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\frac{e^{i\\theta}}{1+\\frac{1}{4}e^{i2\\theta}}+\\frac{e^{-i\\theta}}{1+\\frac{1}{4}e^{-i2\\theta}}\\right)\\\\  &amp;= \\frac{5(e^{i\\theta}+e^{-i\\theta})}{17+4e^{i2\\theta}+4e^{-i2\\theta}}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"601\" height=\"144\" />\n</p><p>Repeating the above process, we find that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/1510ef5525d606ffc83ae44b4d5f871ced2a30d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2i(e^{i2\\theta}-e^{-i2\\theta})}{17+4e^{i2\\theta}+4e^{-i2\\theta}},\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"41\" /> the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3f133b56435d7eab201281bb2ad4a2114f79e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{16+2(e^{i2\\theta}+e^{-i2\\theta})}{17+4e^{i2\\theta}+4e^{-i2\\theta}},\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"41\" /> and finally, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c0338117beb0473ba01185de9873da8ee54fd7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3i(e^{i\\theta}-e^{-i\\theta})}{17+4e^{i2\\theta}+4e^{-i2\\theta}}.\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Converting back to trigonometric form, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e20d01bc2cd2544141992dc6a745f5a89b4e7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{7}&amp;=\\frac{10\\cos{\\theta}-4\\sin{2\\theta}}{16+4\\cos{2\\theta}-6\\sin{\\theta}}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{5\\cos{\\theta}-2\\sin{2\\theta}}{8+2\\cos{2\\theta}-3\\sin{\\theta}}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"228\" height=\"88\" /> Using the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> double identity and simplifying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4ec39fc84feb41f0f0395ea59d19001b04cc58.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{7}=\\frac{\\cos{\\theta}(5-4\\sin{\\theta})}{10-4\\sin^2{\\theta}-3\\sin{\\theta}}.\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"42\" /> Factoring the denominator, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/67459fba1c46908ed32b29023e16ca2424d84d12.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10-4\\sin^2{\\theta}-3\\sin{\\theta}=(5-4\\sin\\theta)(2+\\sin\\theta).\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"20\" /> Simplifying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e5ec24bf1d3512dff2d232102a62c3111648f3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{7}&amp;= \\frac{\\cos{\\theta}(5-4\\sin{\\theta})}{(5-4\\sin\\theta)(2+\\sin\\theta)}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{2+\\sin\\theta}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"233\" height=\"91\" /> We set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cc6cd401ab7d1f6f198d8b36a1e53d6403555e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta$\" width=\"34\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and by the Pythagorean Identity, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c9425c41e8f9ca59c1f4fcac56f9a8a34b58da4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57x^2+32x-17=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"160\" height=\"16\" />. This factors into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/852f3fda4e17bf606923aab5a81e1b9eec1b3a73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(19x+17)(3x-1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />, which yields the 2 solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45cb14f966029b511cb0c767cd0c0b266766030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac{17}{19}, x=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"129\" height=\"38\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a76c902fda99f53670bb31b932dae8b76cd42216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi\\leq\\theta&lt;2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />, the latter root is erroneous, and we are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5758efbaa72ea768218fa2ce55cb9445cb2db5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta=-\\frac{17}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904c49894e7b5e64875e93edfc386cc3b79bd389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17+19=\\boxed{036}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ASAB\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Follow solution 3, up to the point of using the geometric series formula\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a5441f1abdef8136ebaf1deae9c0ba93f4ce4e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q+iP=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}-\\frac{Qi\\cos(\\theta)}{2}}\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Moving everything to the other side, and considering only the imaginary part, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2ed81cb047ef636e5942f80c43c5f1a14fbd0c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Pi+\\frac{Pi}{2}\\sin\\theta-\\frac{Qi}{2}\\cos\\theta = 0\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>We can then write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/14996eb26780c826380018539c7db982cb157481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = 2 \\sqrt{2} k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfba6104bd8b706e3d6cb1bd0a6aa27befa570dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = 7k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" />, (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e382be12e5c9272e25f196b60dab1752cd07077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />). Thus, we can substitute and divide out by k.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18dd4a1de1f0fb3fe377b4224e86c0e69081f2e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta-\\frac{7}{2}\\cos\\theta\\ =\\ 0\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf80c0a717f148db28f131df6d3b79cfc9159db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta-\\frac{7}{2}\\sqrt{1-\\sin^{2}\\theta}=\\ 0\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fca70a0870f65a9c79dc7911023d8d56e73094f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta\\ =\\frac{7}{2}\\left(\\sqrt{1-\\sin^{2}\\theta}\\right)\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/4/b742554ba95d3e47a08ad7fc5cad4b5d5ba51bfe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8+8\\sin\\theta+2\\sin^{2}\\theta=\\frac{49}{4}-\\frac{49}{7}\\sin^{2}\\theta\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad48d289f8a318d4e62e1dfab448872c19d1c254.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{57}{4}\\sin^{2}\\theta+8\\sin\\theta-\\frac{17}{4} = 0\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee48ca06df659a9219e87d3de240bcf086bfdaf3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[57\\sin^{2}\\theta+32\\sin\\theta-17 = 0\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a52d6c9e0a4a0ce7fca4d4d54154836ca0069c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(3\\sin\\theta-1\\right)\\left(19\\sin\\theta+17\\right) = 0\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f4b10f1bbab2d159a8c5749bc1163291517b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\le \\theta &lt; 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b639ffe4d4276f5ffc2aaa96d38b5eb318c28e5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />, and thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/f/d4f4115f045a3202f753134cf2ff0935e8914df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta = \\frac{-17}{19} \\implies \\boxed{036}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"185\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>-Alexlikemath\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/036u51CF-EQ?si=SHTrTwSg3LMnE_yH\">https://youtu.be/036u51CF-EQ?si=SHTrTwSg3LMnE_yH</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=adaCVexm6qQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=adaCVexm6qQ</a>\n- Jonathan Ding (Art of Learning Math)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I\" title=\"2013 AIME I\">2013 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017231244\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.059 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 683/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1790/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 112/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 24569/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.513      1 -total\n 58.48%    7.318      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.09%    4.891      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11851:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017231244 and revision id 272635. Rendering